use std
into libm.amni
namespace libm
driver ../../test/libm/drive_libm.amni
dialect rust

A port of libm 0.2.16 (musl) single-precision `atan2f`, `atanf`, `sincosf`, `sinf`, `cosf` and `hypotf`, with their kernels. Float bits are read with `binary::f32_bits` and built with `binary::f32_from_bits` (import `binary`). `floor` comes from `math` (import `math`). Floating-point exception side effects (`force_eval!`) are dropped. Every value marked f32 is computed in f32 arithmetic, rounding at each operation. Every value marked f64 is `real`. A cast from f32 to `real` widens exactly. A cast from `real` to f32 rounds to nearest.

struct `Ipio2Row` with one field `v int`. It holds one row of the 2/pi bit table. Each row is 24 bits of 2/pi: row i is the bits from 24*i to 24*i+23 after the binary point.

